WHY THE SPLIT
-------------

0BSD is deliberately the "no strings at all" licence: it grants permission to
use, copy, modify and distribute with no attribution requirement whatsoever.
That is the right posture for cryptographic library code, which should be as
easy as possible to vendor, adapt, and re-license downstream.

It is the wrong posture for the prose. The documentation here — particularly
the "How it works" chapters and the build-it-yourself study path — is original
explanatory work, and the expectation is that someone who learns from it and
goes on to write their own implementation says so. CC BY 4.0 makes that
expectation explicit rather than leaving it as an unenforceable hope.

The requirement is only credit. Commercial use, adaptation, translation, and
redistribution are all permitted.


